    """Combine two count dicts by summing values for shared keys.

    Inputs are not modified. Keys from a come first (in their order),
    followed by keys only present in b (in their order).

    >>> merge_count_dicts({'x': 1, 'y': 2}, {'y': 3, 'z': 4})
