    """Summarize how dict new differs from dict old.

    Return {'added': [...], 'removed': [...], 'changed': [...]}, where added
    are keys only in new, removed are keys only in old, and changed are keys
    in both with unequal values. Each list is sorted.

    >>> describe_dict_changes({'a': 1, 'b': 2}, {'b': 3, 'c': 4})
    {'added': ['c'], 'removed': ['a'], 'changed': ['b']}
    >>> describe_dict_changes({}, {})
